                <pb facs="0561" n="459" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg459"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dennis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to President Diaz</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-11-25"><hi rendition="#italic">November 25,
                        1926</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: Completing the memorandum
                    of our conversation of November 17, transmitted to you with my letter of the
                    18th, I am enclosing a further memorandum embodying some of the points discussed
                    with you in that conversation and further elaborated in subsequent
                    conversations.</p>
                <p>I should greatly appreciate any corrections which you may see fit to make to this
                    memorandum, in the absence of which I shall consider the impressions I have set
                    down as substantially accurate.</p>
                <p>With the assurance [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lawrence Dennis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
